{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-319922" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $AC-BC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -4\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n|  |  | $4$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AC-BC=\\,\\,$ |  | $0$ | $-4$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} | $4$ |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-319922" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply the distributive law on the right:\n\n$$\nAC-BC=(A-B)C.\n$$\n\nSo, compute $A-B$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-B & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4{I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC-BC & =(A-B)C \\\\  & =(4{I}_{3})C \\\\  & =4C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-319922" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "442e8807297dc2494084b95676f504ca51d5b48601a0223f31f0024d65b046fe"} {"question" "q-319922" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-319922" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-319922" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-319922" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-319922" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-319922" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-319922" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-319922" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-75635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $CB+CA$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -\\sqrt{3} & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-75635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply the distributive law \n\n$$\nCB+CA=C(B+A).\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $B+A$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B+A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -\\sqrt{3} & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4{I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CB+CA & =C(B+A) \\\\  & =C\\cdot 4{I}_{3} \\\\  & =4C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-75635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "442e8807297dc2494084b95676f504ca51d5b48601a0223f31f0024d65b046fe"} {"question" "q-75635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-75635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-75635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-275518" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $AC+BC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -6 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 8 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{5} & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n|  |  | $8\\sqrt{5}$ | $-4$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AC+BC=\\,\\,$ |  | $0$ | {{field-2}} | $16$ |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} | $12$ | $20$ |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-275518" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nAC+BC=(A+B)C.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A+B$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -6 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 8 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4{I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC+BC & =(A+B)C \\\\  & =4{I}_{3}C \\\\  & =4C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8\\sqrt{5} & -4 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 4\\sqrt{3} & 16 \\\\ -8 & 12 & 20\\text{ }\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-275518" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "442e8807297dc2494084b95676f504ca51d5b48601a0223f31f0024d65b046fe"} {"question" "q-275518" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/refe