30af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-319886" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nAC+BC=(A+B)C.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A+B$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC+BC & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & \\sqrt{6} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 3\\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-319886" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "442e8807297dc2494084b95676f504ca51d5b48601a0223f31f0024d65b046fe"} {"question" "q-319886" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-319886" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-319886" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-319886" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-319886" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-319886" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\sqrt{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-42259" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-42259" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, and $C$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 3$ matrix, which will require finding $9$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $2$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-42259" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "442e8807297dc2494084b95676f504ca51d5b48601a0223f31f0024d65b046fe"} {"question" "q-42259" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-42259" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -2 \\\\ -15 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -2 \\\\ 15 & -7 \\\\ 9 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned