ed}-2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-18 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 42 & 0 & -21 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-42001" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "442e8807297dc2494084b95676f504ca51d5b48601a0223f31f0024d65b046fe"} {"question" "q-42001" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-42001" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-144"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-18 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 42 & 0 & -21 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ 42 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 18 & 9 \\\\ 21 & 7 & -42 \\\\ 8 & 2 & -6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}21 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 18 & 9 & -42 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-42001" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-18 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 42 & 0 & -21 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-41981" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-41981" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, and $C$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $1\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $2$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $4$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 11\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 11\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-41981" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "442e8807297dc2494084b95676f504ca51d5b48601a0223f31f0024d65b0