is a $1\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $1\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding only $1$ entry, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 3$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6\\cdot (-1)+(-2)\\cdot 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6-6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-12\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $(AB)$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)\\,C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-12\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-24 & 48 & -60\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-320021" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "442e8807297dc2494084b95676f504ca51d5b48601a0223f31f0024d65b046fe"} {"question" "q-320021" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-320021" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-24"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "fi