imes 1$ matrix, $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix, and $C$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $1\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding only $1$ entry.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ 24 \\\\ 36\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-42002" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "442e8807297dc2494084b95676f504ca51d5b48601a0223f31f0024d65b046fe"} {"question" "q-42002" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-42002" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ 24 \\\\ 36\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ 30 \\\\ 36\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-36\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 30 & 24\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-42002" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ 24 \\\\ 36\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-75664" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $A$ and $B$  are $4\\times 4$ matrices,  and ${I}_{4}$ is the $4\\times 4$ identity matrix,  which of the following statements are always true?\n\n- $AB=BA$\n- $A{I}_{4}={I}_{4}A$\n- $A(B+{I}_{4})=AB+A$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-75664" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is true. Matrix multiplication is not commutative in general, however, multiplication by the identity matrix is always commutative. In this case, we have  $A{I}_{4}={I}_{4}A=A.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B+{I}_{4})=AB+A{I}_{4}=AB+A$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statements II  and III are true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-75664" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "442e8807297dc2494084b95676f504ca51d5b48601a0223f31f0024d65b046fe"} {"question" "q-75664" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-75664" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-75664" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-42264" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $2\\times 2$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\n- $AB=BA$\n- $(AB)C=A(BC)$\n- $A(B-C)=(B-C)A$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-42264" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is true. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C=A(BC)$ in general.\n\n- Statement III is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $A(B-C)\\ne (B-C)A$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-42264" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "442e8807297dc2494084b95676f504ca51d5b48601a0223f31f0024d65b046fe"} {"question" "q-42264" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-42264" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-42264" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-130478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $7\\times 7$ matrices which of the following statements are always true? \n\n- $(CA)B=C(BA)$\n- $(A+A)B=2AB$\n- $CB=BC$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-130478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I  is false. Matrix multiplication is associative and  $(CA)B=C(AB)$ is always true. However,  matrix multiplication is not commutative,   $AB\\ne BA$ in general. Therefore, $(CA)B\\ne C(BA)$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+A)B=AB+AB=2AB$ is always true.\n\n- Statement III is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative in general, so $CB\\ne BC$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-130478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "442e8807297dc2494084b95676f504ca51d5b48601a0223f31f0024d65b046fe"} {"question" "q-130478" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-130478" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-130478" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-130455" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $6\\times 6$ matrices which of the following statements are always true? \n\n- $A(BC)=(AB)C$\n- $A(B-C)=AB-CA$\n- $CA=AC$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-130455" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is associative and  $A(BC)=(AB)C$ is always true.\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B-C)=AB-AC,$ but $AC\\ne CA$ because matrix multiplication is not commutative in general.\n\n- Statement III  is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $CA\\ne AC$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statement  I is true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/state.json" "file_sha256" "70a8f7526f69a86b8b2e165d85be18374cc9cd6830af982ad41ddca69349071b"} {"question" "q-130455" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993704/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "442e8807297dc2494084b95676f504ca51d5b48601a0223f31f0024d65b046fe"} {"question" "q-130455" "field" "selection" "at